# Combat Retaliation — counter & consumed flag

Creatures normally retaliate **once per turn** (until refreshed). The engine tracks retaliation with **two fields** on the outer combat unit:

| Offset | Creature-relative | Role |
|---|---|---|
| **`+0xC4`** | `*(int*)(ICombatCreature* this - 0x80)` | **Retaliation counter** — `stub_return_false_e4` (`+0x1E4`) requires `>= 1` on the main retaliate path; decremented when a retaliate is consumed |
| **`+0xC8`** | `*(byte*)(ICombatCreature* this - 0x7C)` via `get_state_flag_7c` (`+0x5C`) | **Consumed flag** — first gate in `FUN_00a5fee0`; also set by lazy property getter `FUN_00bdfcf0` |

| `+0xC8` | `get_state_flag_7c()` (`+0x5C`) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `0` | returns `0` | **Can** retaliate (if counter also allows) |
| non-zero (`1`) | returns non-zero | Retaliation **consumed** — cannot retaliate until reset |

**Patching:** decrementing the **counter** (same as `func_CombatCreature_RetVoidE8` / vtable `+0x1E8`) is sufficient to block melee retaliates until turn refresh. Writing **`+0xC8` alone does not** — confirmed by `ShockingBolts.cpp`.

Heroes always report “can retaliate” via stub `func_CombatHero_ReturnFalse` @ `0x00BBF550` (slot always `0`).

## Vtable read — `get_state_flag_7c` (`CombatUnit` slot `+0x5C`)

Documented in `src/structs/CombatUnit.h`. Creature impl:

| Slot | Impl | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `+0x5C` | `0x008A0F20` | **get_state_flag_7c** — `func_CombatCreature_GetStateFlag7C` |

```c
// func_CombatCreature_GetStateFlag7C @ 0x008A0F20
return *(byte*)(ICombatCreature* this - 0x7C);  // == outer unit +0xC8
```

**Read-only query** through the vtable. Does **not** consume the flag.

Do not confuse with **outer unit `+0x7C`**: that offset holds a **hero/advmap pointer** (see `ModAtbReset.cpp`), not this flag.

## Counter gate — `stub_return_false_e4` (`CombatUnit` slot `+0x1E4`)

`func_CombatCreature_StubReturnFalseE4` @ `0x008A10E0`:

```c
if (*(int*)(ICombatCreature* this - 0x80) < 1)
    return 0;
// …fierce-retaliation extras…
return 1;
```

Used in `FUN_00a5fee0` @ `0x00A60173`: counter `>= 1` → proceed toward `"COMBAT_WILL_RETALIATE"`; counter `< 1` → `"COMBAT_NO_RETALIATE"` (unless ability `0x68`).

## Attack prediction — `FUN_00a5fee0` @ `0x00A5FEE0`

Called from **`FUN_00a63020` @ `0x00A63020`** (attack damage prediction; sets `"retaliate"` / `"COMBAT_WILL_RETALIATE"` / `"COMBAT_PREDICTION_YES|NO"`).

Gates on the **defender** (in order on the default path):

1. `defender->vtable[+0x5C]()` (`+0xC8` byte) — if set → `"COMBAT_NO_RETALIATE"`
2. …ability / buff checks…
3. `defender->vtable[+0x1E4]()` — counter at `+0xC4` / `this - 0x80`

Other ability-related prediction strings from the same function:

| Ability | ID | Role in `FUN_00a5fee0` |
|---|---|---|
| **No enemy retaliation** | `5` (`ABILITY_NO_ENEMY_RETALIATION`) | Attacker `has_ability(5)` → `"COMBAT_NO_ENEMY_RETALIATE"` |
| **Ranged retaliate** | `34` (`0x22`, `ABILITY_RANGED_RETALIATE`) | Ranged attack && !defender `has_ability(0x22)` → `"COMBAT_NO_SHOOTER_RETALIATE"` |
| **Unlimited retaliation** | `6` | **Not checked** in this function |

Related prediction strings (same function): `"COMBAT_NO_RETALIATE_COVARDICE"`, `"COMBAT_NO_RETALIATE_TO_FAST_ATTACKER"`, `"COMBAT_NO_BLIND_RETALIATE"`, `"COMBAT_NO_HYPNOTIZE_RETALIATE"`, etc.

## Retaliation execution

```
func_CreatureAttackEffects @ 0x00A65260
  └─ FUN_00a64e90 @ 0x00A64E90
       ├─ FUN_00a5fee0(...)              // prediction gate (+0x5C, +0x1E4, …)
       └─ FUN_00a646b0 @ 0x00A646B0     // retaliation strike (defender → attacker)
            ├─ vtable +0x1E8             // func_CombatCreature_RetVoidE8 — decrement counter
            ├─ FUN_00a62890 @ 0x00A62890
            ├─ FUN_00a673c0 @ 0x00A673C0
            ├─ FUN_00a629b0 @ 0x00A629B0
            └─ FUN_00a64120 @ 0x00A64120  // skips bonus hooks if defender +0x5C set
```

`func_CombatAttackWithRedirects` @ `0x00A65D50` eventually enters `func_CreatureAttackEffects`.

## Consume — counter decrement (`+0x1E8`)

**Primary melee consume** — `func_CombatCreature_RetVoidE8` @ `0x008A1120`, vtable slot `+0x1E8`. Called from `FUN_00a646b0` **before** counter-strike damage:

```c
if (!has_ability(6)) {
    *(int*)(ICombatCreature* this - 0x80) -= 1;   // outer +0xC4
    func_EnqueueUnitRefresh(creature_this);       // 0x0050C020 — DLL: enqueue_unit_refresh
}
```

Ability **6** (Unlimited Retaliation) skips the decrement; perk mapping in `ModAbilities.cpp` (`0xDA` → ability `6`).

### Secondary consume — `+0xC8` property getter `FUN_00bdfcf0` @ `0x00BDFCF0`

Lazy property pattern on **outer** unit pointer; sets `+0xC8` to `1` on first read. Does **not** decrement `+0xC4`. Duplicate thunks ~`0x00AB0DB0` / `0x00AB0F30` / `0x00AB11F0`. Helper `FUN_00bdfa50` @ `0x00BDFA50`.

### Spawn default

**`FUN_00a83860` @ `0x00A83860`**: `*(byte*)(param_1 + 0xC8) = 1` on unit ctor — starts as “cannot retaliate” until combat turn refresh clears it.

## Reset — allow retaliate again next turn

| Function | Address | Action |
|---|---|---|
| **`FUN_00beca60`** | `0x00BECA60` | `param_1[0x32] = 0` — clears `+0xC8` byte |
| **`FUN_00bec920`** | `0x00BEC920` | copy ctor path also clears `+0xC8` |
| Property vtable | `0x00E86F10` / `0x00E86F3C` | virtual turn-reset family |

Turn refresh also restores the retaliation counter (counter back to usable state). **`func_CombatCreature_OnTimelineRefresh` @ `0x008A6210`** clears side-tile flags when `+0x5C` is set — does **not** reset unit `+0xC8` or counter directly.

## Shocking Bolts (`src/patches/ShockingBolts.cpp`)

`PERK_SHOCKING_BOLTS` — lightning with stun consumes the **target's** retaliation so it cannot counter on subsequent **melee** attacks until its next turn. Creatures cannot retaliate against spells; hook is only on the existing stun branch.

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Hook | `0x004E6B19` → return `0x004E6B1E` inside `func_ApplySpellDamageWithStun` (before `func_CheckLightningSpellStun`) |
| Registers @ fork | `EDI` = caster outer, `EBP` = target |
| Consume | if `*(int*)(target - 0x80) > 0` → decrement; `enqueue_unit_refresh(target - 0x148)` |
| Skips | heroes (`get_unit_kind != 1`); no `+0xC8` write |

